  "note": "A2 liść · sibling of a2_feelings, same shape. Teaches 11 new describing adjectives plus their feminine forms; masculine is the citation form, feminine is on the board too. Singular only, no plural forms, imperfective only. ANCHORS, never re-taught: ładny (opposite of brzydki), wysoki (opposite of niski), młody, stary, dobry, zły, nowy, duży, mały. TONE RULE for this pack: brzydki, głupi, gruby and chudy are never aimed at a named family member. brzydki goes on weather and clothes, głupi on a film / a game, gruby and chudy on a cat, a dog, a cow and a book, niski on a table and a price. słaby is used of the speaker himself and of weak tea. The kind words (miły, mądry, silny) are the ones that get the family: siostra, córka, mama, kelner. Adjectives take no gender badge (that field is for nouns).",
